WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.694
Use this checkpoint to test the contracts A
comparison such as

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:11.617
age greater than parentheses requires one scalar
value IN expects

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:17.582
a one-column set EXISTS only needs to know whether
any row exists

00:00:19.323 --> 00:00:25.154
And a subquery is correlated when it references the
current outer row If

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:29.983
you can identify these contracts the syntax becomes
much easier to reconstruct
